        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: అభ్యంతరం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అభ్యంతరం — abhyantaraṁ — \"an objection\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మీకు ఏమైనా అభ్యంతరం ఉందా? mīku ēmainā abhyantaraṁ undā? Do you have any objection?"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: అభ్యంతరాలు, abhyantarālu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A polite opening: మీకు అభ్యంతరం (abhyantaraṁ) లేకపోతే, if you have no objection."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అభ్యంతరం (abhyantaraṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit abhyantara, \"interior\", and as a noun \"the inside\" (CDIAL 544). In Telugu the word has taken the sense of an objection."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
